// HAND-WRITTEN — not generated by `tools/kt_generate.py`, which only writes the factions on
// Warhammer Community's download list.
//
// COMPANIONS OF THE EMPEROR (Adeptus Custodes) — a homebrew kill team, transcribed from
// https://ktdash.app/killteams/HBR-dOb7j-2 via that site's JSON API. Everything below comes
// from that source EXCEPT the Custodian Warden, which is marked where it appears.
//
// Two things the team's own faction rule decides, rather than me:
//   - `acts: 2` — "may be activated twice during the turning point ... stays ready while it can
//     still be activated a second time".
//   - `kv: 2`  — "when a friendly operative dies, it counts as two operatives and your opponent
//     scores Victory Points accordingly". A three-model kill team would otherwise hand the enemy
//     grade 3 for three kills.
//
// The source lists 17 equipment entries, 13 of which are the UNIVERSAL equipment the app already
// ships in `UNIVERSAL_EQUIPMENT` and concatenates onto every equipment deck. Only the four
// faction ones are here; importing the rest would show each twice.
//
// Weapon profiles ride on the datacards because this team has no printed cards and the player
// view shows no operative stats — unlike the 48 extracted factions, where both are true.
//
// Weapons are grouped into LOADOUTS. The source lists each weapon as its own row, so the shield
// never appeared beside the sword it comes with — only the composition rule pairs them, and that
// is not in the weapon data. Shield Captain, Custodian Guard and Venatari each pick one of two;
// Blade Champion and the Warden have no choice to make, so their weapons are listed flat.
import type { Datacard, RefCard } from '../compendium'
